Keep a shared counts as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared ends as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared possible as 0.
To lengthen from value (a whole number).
Repeat while item value of counts is more than 0.
The onward is 0.
If value is more than 0 and item (value minus 1) of ends is more than 0, set onward to 1.
If onward is 1, set item (value minus 1) of ends to item (value minus 1) of ends minus 1.
If onward is 1, set item value of ends to item value of ends plus 1.
If onward is 1, set item value of counts to item value of counts minus 1.
The fresh is 0.
If onward is 0 and value is at most 7 and item (value plus 1) of counts is more than 0 and item (value plus 2) of counts is more than 0, set fresh to 1.
If fresh is 1, set item value of counts to item value of counts minus 1.
If fresh is 1, set item (value plus 1) of counts to item (value plus 1) of counts minus 1.
If fresh is 1, set item (value plus 2) of counts to item (value plus 2) of counts minus 1.
If fresh is 1, set item (value plus 2) of ends to item (value plus 2) of ends plus 1.
If onward is 0 and fresh is 0, set possible to 0, set item value of counts to 0.

The numbers is a list of 1, 2, 3, 3, 4, and 5.
For every value from 0 to 9.
Place 0 into counts.
Place 0 into ends.

For each value in numbers.
Set item value of counts to item value of counts plus 1.

Set possible to 1.
For every value from 0 to 9.
Lengthen from value.
If possible is 0, stop.

If possible is 1, show true, otherwise show false.
